From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:07:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Use the trivial country
 code map for Wi-Fi

The BCM4388 on the T8132 laptops takes ISO 3166 country codes as its own
codes (revision 0), as on every other Apple Silicon machine, but its
node lacked brcm,ccode-map-trivial. brcmfmac then has no translation
for the chip and drops every regulatory hint: the country an access
point advertises, iw reg set or wireless-regdom. The firmware stays on
its worldwide default (phy country 99) where macOS on the same Mac runs
the access point's country (US).

Add the property, as the t8103, t8112, t8122, t600x, t603x and t604x
device trees have it.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
(cherry picked from commit e0bf994300b6f27d6bc0b15d77514e1ce9b7f7e2)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-jxxx.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-jxxx.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-jxxx.dtsi
index 03a129758b..3f378b1ffc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-jxxx.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-jxxx.dtsi
@@ -470,5 +470,6 @@ wifi0: wifi@0,0 {
 		reg = <0x10000 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
 		local-mac-address = [00 00 00 00 00 00];
 		apple,antenna-sku = "XX";
+		brcm,ccode-map-trivial;
 	};
 };
